+ * R first SwapEnd record words, F frames.
+ *
+ * v399: PMU calibration. v398 read DPU CONFIGURATION/STATUS = 0/0 at publish
+ * and at the first SwapEnd. The loader Linux (stock dpu20, "display supports
+ * hibernation mode") leaves DECON0 in command-mode hibernation when TWRP is
+ * idle: DSIM in ULPS, D-PHY isolated, pm_runtime_put -> pd-dpu off, panel on
+ * with its own frame memory. To tell a real power-off from a bad read,
+ * n10_disp_probe() now first reads always-on PMU registers that must be on
+ * (pmucal flexpmu_cal_cpu_exynos9820.h: CLUSTER0_CPU0 CONFIGURATION/STATUS
+ * 0x1000/0x1004, CLUSTER0_NONCPU_STATUS 0x1204) plus record-only values
+ * (CLUSTER0_CPU1 0x1084, CLUSTER1_CPU0 0x1304, CLUSTER2_CPU0 0x1504,
+ * CLUSTER2_NONCPU 0x1604, MIPI D-PHY isolation 0x70c/0x710 of the DSIM0
+ * m4s4/m4s0 PHYs (exynos9820.dts), DPU 0x1e00/0x1e04) through one PMU
+ * mapping (0x15860000, reads only); one N399C line, cal = CPU0 and NONCPU0
+ * status bit 0 set. DECON0 / IDMA / SysMMU are read only when cal = 1 and the
+ * DPU status bit 0 is set (v398: status bit only); an uncalibrated PMU read
+ * skips them ("N398E skip pmu_uncal"). Arm, frame and write path unchanged.
+ *
+ * v399 (b): n10_disp_arm() also accepts IDMA format 1 (ABGR8888), the format
+ * the Linux fbdev pan (decon_pan_display, used by TWRP and by the v399 loader
+ * keep-on) programs on the fb window. dpu20 gives no byte order for it
+ * (decon_enable programs BGRA8888 on the same buffer, the fb var says red
+ * 16-23), so the order is checked at run time from the alpha byte of the
+ * opaque frame Linux left in the window buffer: 64 pixels are read through the
+ * write-combined buffer mapping (reads only); alpha 0xff in byte 3 of all 64
+ * and not in byte 0 = bytes R,G,B,A (copy swaps R/B), alpha 0xff in byte 0 of
+ * all 64 and not in byte 3 = bytes A,B,G,R (copy rotates by one byte); alpha
+ * is forced to 0xff for format 1 (per-pixel alpha); anything else stays
+ * read-only (N398A why=order). One N399O line. Formats 2/3/6/7 unchanged.
+ */
